    {
      "title": "Why is Ukraine's ex-defence minister calling for wartime elections?",
      "link": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/c62eyn5ggnzo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
      "description": "Mykhailo Fedorov has called for elections, without addressing concerns over how they could be held while at war.",
      "source_name": "BBC World News",
      "published": "2026-08-19T15:38:38"
    },
    {
      "title": "Sacking turns former Zelenskyy loyalist into potent political opponent",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/19/mykhailo-fedorov-zelenskyy-loyalist-opponent-ukraine",
      "description": "<p>Mykhailo Fedorov’s blistering critique comes at a time of growing pressure for democratic renewal in Ukraine</p><p>For more than a month, demonstrators have gathered in Ivan Franko Square outside Volodymyr Zelenskyy’s office. The <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/jul/17/zelenskyy-defends-sacking-ukraine-defence-minister-mykhailo-fedorov\">protesters have been chanting a name</a> – not that of Ukraine’s embattled president but that of the man he recently <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/jul/22/volodymyr-zelenskyy-pressure-reinstate-sacked-defence-minister-mykhailo-fedorov\">sacked as defence minister</a>, Mykhailo Fedorov. On Sunday evening, 2,000 people marched along Khreshchatyk, Kyiv’s main boulevard, waving cardboard banners in support of their ousted hero.</p><p>Zelenskyy has refused to reinstate Fedorov, who during his six months in the job was widely seen as an effective and reforming figure. On Wednesday, Ukraine’s parliament, the Rada, <a href=\"https://kyivindependent.com/parliament-votes-through-yevhen-khmara-to-succeed-fedorov-as-defense-minister/\">voted to approve a successor</a> as defence minister, Yevhen Khmara. The move shows that Fedorov has been shut out from government permanently, and confirms his transition from trusted insider and Zelenskyy loyalist to a potent political opponent.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/19/mykhailo-fedorov-zelenskyy-loyalist-opponent-ukraine\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-19T15:52:04"
    },
    {
      "title": "Protests in Kyiv back ex-defence minister Fedorov’s call for elections",
      "link": "https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/8/19/19-08-reported-audreymacalpine-kyiv-ua?traffic_source=rss",
      "description": "Ukrainians in Kyiv held a protest in support of ousted defence Minister Mykailo Fedorov.",
      "source_name": "Al Jazeera All News",
      "published": "2026-08-19T19:09:53"
    },
    {
      "title": "Ousted Ukraine Def Min urges wartime election, warning of governance crisis",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/ousted-ukraine-def-min-urges-wartime-election-warning-of-governance-crisis-126081900580_1.html",
      "description": "Ukraine's ousted Defence Minister Mykhailo Fedorov called Tuesday for elections to be held even as the war against Russia continues, saying the country was gripped by a crisis of governance.\nThe move by one of President Volodymyr Zelenskyy's most loyal and longstanding team members until recently could become the most significant internal challenge Zelenskyy has faced since Russia's full-scale invasion.\nThe appeal came in a video address posted to YouTube by Fedorov, who lost his post in July.\n\"We must find a legal, safe, and realistic mechanism that will allow Ukraine to restore a full democratic process even amid a prolonged war,\" Fedorov said.\nZelenskyy's office did not immediately comment on Fedorov's address.\nUkrainian law prohibits elections while the country is under martial law, which was imposed on Feb. 24, 2022, the day that the Russian invasion began.\nFedorov said the country was facing a systemic crisis in how it is governed, arguing the current system is oriented tow",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-08-19T18:04:13"
    }
  ]
